INT. ROWING BOATHOUSE - EARLY MORNING

Long wooden shells hang from the rafters like the ribs of a whale. Water slaps the dock outside. Mist presses against the glass. The smell of varnish and river mud.

COACH HESTER LINDQVIST-AMOAH, 60s, thermos in one hand and a stopwatch in the other, sits on an upturned oar rack. Across the room, her only remaining athlete, PASCAL ODUYA-REYNAUD, 20s, wraps tape around a blistered palm. They do not look at each other. A kettle ticks on a hotplate.

HESTER
(to the room)
Tide's slack at six-fifteen.

PASCAL
(to his hand)
I know.

HESTER
(to no one)
Wind from the west. Light.

PASCAL
I read the board.

She sips from the thermos. He bites the end of the tape. The kettle begins to whistle. Neither moves. Hester sighs and rises, pulls the kettle off the hotplate, pours two mugs.

She sets one on the bench beside him. He doesn't take it. She sits again.

HESTER
Sixteen minutes on the water. Then back. Then breakfast.

PASCAL
Fine.

HESTER
Don't "fine" me.

PASCAL
Okay, then.

HESTER
Okay is worse.

He smiles faintly. Takes the mug. Warms his hands on it. Mist drifts in through a crack in the doorframe.

HESTER (CONT'D)
(to the room again)
Anyone else coming?

PASCAL
You know no one's coming.

HESTER
(muttering)
I know.

Pascal sips. Looks at the shells overhead. His eyes trace the hull of an eight, then of a single.

PASCAL
Remember when we filled this place?

HESTER
We had fourteen on the squad. And a cox who ate her megaphone.

PASCAL
(smiling)
Camille.

HESTER
Camille. Yes.

Quiet. The water slaps. A gull cries.

PASCAL
Coach.

HESTER
Hm?

PASCAL
If I miss the cut --

HESTER
You won't.

PASCAL
But if.

She turns the stopwatch over in her hand. Reads the back, where someone long ago scratched initials.

HESTER
Then we row anyway.

He nods. Finishes his tea. Sets the mug on the bench and stands. Pulls on his gloves. She stands too. Together they lift a single shell from its cradle. It swings, light as a leaf.

HESTER (CONT'D)
(to the room)
Mind the door.

PASCAL
(to the boat)
Easy.

They carry it out toward the dock, the mist closing behind.
